ration. The best practice is to use \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"exponential backoff with jitter\"}],\":\"]}]\n6c:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Exponential Backoff\"}],\": Increase the delay between retries exponentially (e.g., 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s). This prevents overwhelming the server with rapid-fire retries if it's in the process of restarting.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Jitter\"}],\": Add a small, random amount of time to each delay. This prevents multiple instances of your application from retrying in lockstep (a \",[\"$\",\"$L64\",null,{\"href\":\"https://e"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"n.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thundering_herd_problem\",\"children\":\"thundering herd problem\"}],\"), which can overload the database.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n6d:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"configure-connection-timeouts\",\"className\":\"anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-extra-tight\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"Configure connection timeouts\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden\",\"href\":\"#configure-connection-timeouts\",\"aria-label\":\"Link to Configure connection timeouts\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":14,\"height\":14,\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 14 14\",\"className\":\"inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3\",\"children\":\"$5a:6:props:children:1:props:children:props:children\"}]}]]}]\n6e:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"A compute restart or cold start on Neon typically takes only a few hundred milliseconds, though in very rare cases it can extend to a few seconds. If